window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>The ocean has always called to me.</b></p> <p>For as long as I can remember, I've felt its whispers beneath my skin, pulling me toward something I can't name. But I never expected the sea to answer back until the day I found the ruins. Until the day they came for me.</p> <p>Now, I'm being hunted for a power I don't understand, for memories that aren't mine. Rescued by a cursed pirate with secrets darker than the deep, a selkie warrior who fights against fate, an exiled guardian sworn to protect me, and a fallen god who refuses to let me go, I'm thrust into a world where magic is as wild as the sea itself.</p> <p>They say I am the key to an ancient prophecy. That I once held the power to raise an empire… or to drown it.</p> <p>But the past is rising, and the Water Gate is stirring beneath the tides.</p> <p>And I must decide, will I fight against the tide of destiny? Or will I become the storm I was always meant to be?</p> <p>Witch Call <i>is a dark, romantic fantasy filled with ancient magic, fated mates, and the untamed power of the sea. Perfect for fans of seductive lore, slow-burn tension, and a heroine who holds the ocean in her veins. It is a why-choose romance where the heroine doesn't have to choose and ends with a HEA. It is part of a connected series, best enjoyed in order, though not necessary.</i></p>"; 
